File Name: SensorDataProcessor.py

Necessary Packages: time, math, collections, csv, scipy

Necessary Modules (files): None

Overview: This file contains methods and classes associated with formatting incoming sensor data. It is accessed from
GloveMonitorWindow.py. It performs operations such as filtering, unit conversions, and
recordings (aside from GloveData.csv, this is created directly from SensorRead3.0).

Methods: Not all methods are associated with a class. The classes are: LowPassFilter, SensorProcessor and GyroRecorder

----------------------------------- LowPassFilter --------------------------------------------------------
__init__ (LowPassFilter): Creates our basic low pass filter object with initial values and other parameters.

update: pushes a value through our filter

----------------------------------- Other (no class) --------------------------------------------------------
Overview: At the same file heirarchy level as 'Technical Addendum', you fill find a folder called Flex_Sensor_Angles.
This was created manually (by testing values at angles and computing 3rd-degree polynomial linear regression in
MATLAB, thumb.m and pointer.m) by me to determine the true finger flex angles corresponding to the input flex sensor
resistance values. These functions implement the conversion from the polynomial outputs of these MATLAB programs.

finger_flex_to_angle: utilizes coefficients calculated for finger flex sensors to approximate joint angles

thumb_flex_to_angle: utilizes coefficients calculated for thumb flex sensors to approximate joint angle


----------------------------------- SensorProcessor --------------------------------------------------------
__init__ (SensorProcessor): Initiates all sensor data lowpass filters and relevant environmental variables
(i.e. sample rate)

_init_filters: creates lowpass filters for all incoming sensor data

update_sample_rate: estimates and updates current sample rate for filters to use

process: filters all data (41 incoming signals) before passing it back to GloveMonitorWindow.py

----------------------------------- GyroRecorder --------------------------------------------------------
Overview: used to make recordings on pure gyroscope data. The files created may be used within the data folder of
gyro_calibration as a means to attempt matrix training on gyroscope hardware error. Specifically, there are two ways
to run this:

1. leave lines 431-440 commented. In this case, record repeated sessions of starting hand at a zeroed,
rested position, recording movement, and returning it to that position before stopping the recording.
Hundreds of recordings performing various movements are usually required.

2. Uncomment lines 431-440. This changes the file names the data is stored to by appending '_s' to the name before
'.csv' . This is used to record sessions of negligible movement so that our gyro_calibration can directly estimate
raw sensor drift.

__init__ (GyroRecorder): Initializes basic variables associated with recording gyroscope sessions. These are used
in the gyro_calibration, data folder (copy contents directly into associated files)

start_episode: initiates recording. Called from GloveMonitorWindow.py

stop_episode: terminates recording. Called from GloveMonitorWindow.py

 record: writes current gyroscope angular velocity values to corresponding csv files, along with timestamps and
 session counter (not used for any practical purpose, useful for visual comprehension of files)
